_coalesce takes a struct fallback for a struct the target requires and the
source has as optional: the fallback, a struct of constants, is written
where the source lacks the struct, and the author declares what it stands
for. 1.0 requires q, whose a nothing can fill where 0.0 lacks q.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	q?: {
		a!: int
	}
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	q: {
		a!: int
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		q: _coalesce(v0_0.q, {
			a: 0
		})
	}
	lacunas: {
		q: [{
			type:    Placeholder
			message: "q was absent; {a: 0} is a placeholder"
		}]
	}
}
-- data/0.0/absent.json --
{}
-- data/0.0/q.json --
{"q": {"a": 3}}
-- data/1.0/q.json --
{"q": {"a": 3}}
-- out/bind --
ok
